# Day 19 - 2026-11-27

## What I learned
- Bandit 26: escape restricted shell (vi :set shell / :shell), then setuid ./bandit27-do
- cat /etc/passwd shows each user's login shell (last field)
- git clone over ssh; from Mac use the real hostname, not localhost
- A repo can contain secrets in plain files
- git log: list of commits (history)
- git show COMMIT: what changed in a commit (+ added, - removed)
- Removing a password in a new commit does NOT remove it: it stays in history
- Real fix: clean history AND rotate the password
